{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --branch && rg -n 'eval-bridge|eval compiler|eval-unit|eval-unit|eval coordinator' docs collab test src | head -200\"","aggregated_output":"## eval-bridge...origin/eval-bridge\n?? collab/yang-php/1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log\n?? collab/yang-php/1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.prompt.md\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794209702000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:26:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_12\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '810,850p;885,920p' /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; rg -n 'U1|U2|U3|signed' collab/yang-clojure/*cc1* | tail -60; rg -n 'plain-data|plain\\\\\\\\?' /tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"                             :duplicate-element\\n                             (+ d 2))\\n        sorted (sort #(compare-canonical-bytes (first %1) (first %2)) wired)\\n        item-buffers (map first sorted)\\n        arr (concat-buffers (cons (write-head 4 (count wired)) item-buffers))]\\n    (concat-buffers [(write-head 6 258) arr])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- meta-bytes\\n  \\\"The bytes of x at depth d, where (build depth) encodes x's own\\n   content starting at that depth. If x carries metadata that survives\\n   stripping, a with-meta frame sits at d and x's content moves two\\n   levels deeper (tag, [meta value]). Stripped values are validated\\n   first (ruling A9); a metadata map carrying its own metadata is\\n   refused (ruling A3).\\\"\\n  [x d build]\\n  (let [m (meta x)]\\n    (if (nil? m)\\n      (build d)\\n      (do (when (some? (meta m))\\n            (refuse :malformed-frame \\\"metadata map carries metadata\\\"))\\n          (doseq [k reader-position-keys\\n                  :when (contains? m k)]\\n            (value-bytes (get m k) (+ d 3)))\\n          (let [kept (apply dissoc m reader-position-keys)]\\n            (if (empty? kept)\\n              (build d)\\n              (let [name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode \\\"clojure/with-meta\\\")\\n                    mb (map-bytes kept (+ d 2))\\n                    vb (build (+ d 2))\\n                    frame-arr (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2)\\n                                               (write-head 3 (bytes/length name-bytes))\\n                                               name-bytes\\n                                               (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2) mb vb])])]\\n                (concat-buffers [(write-head 6 27) frame-arr]))))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- identifier-bytes\\n  \\\"Tag 27 at depth d over [name [ns name]]: the components at d+3.\\\"\\n  [tag-name-str x d]\\n  (deep! (+ d 3) :unsupported-value)\\n  [x d]\\n  (cond\\n    (nil? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value) (bytes/from-vector [0xf6]))\\n    (boolean? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value) (bytes/from-vector [(if x 0xf5 0xf4)]))\\n    (string? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value)\\n                    (let [ub (host text/utf8-encode (check-text x))]\\n                      (concat-buffers [(write-head 3 (bytes/length ub)) ub])))\\n    (keyword? x) (identifier-bytes \\\"dao.jing/keyword\\\" x d)\\n    (symbol? x) (meta-bytes x d #(identifier-bytes \\\"dao.jing/symbol\\\" x %))\\n    (byte-payload? x) (do (deep! d :unsupported-value)\\n                          (let [len (bytes/length x)\\n                                head (write-head 2 len)\\n                                out (bytes/alloc (+ (bytes/length head) len))]\\n                            (bytes/copy! head 0 out 0 (bytes/length head))\\n                            (bytes/copy! x 0 out (bytes/length head) len)\\n                            out))\\n    (numeric? x) (number-bytes x d)\\n    (record? x) (refuse :unsupported-value \\\"record\\\")\\n    (map? x) (meta-bytes x d #(map-bytes x %))\\n    (vector? x) (meta-bytes x d (fn [d]\\n                                  (deep! d :unsupported-value)\\n                                  (let [items (mapv #(value-bytes % (inc d)) x)]\\n                                    (concat-buffers (cons (write-head 4 (count items)) items)))))\\n    (set? x) (meta-bytes x d #(set-bytes x %))\\n    (or (list? x) (seq? x)) (meta-bytes x d #(list-bytes x %))\\n    :else (refuse :unsupported-value (type-name x))))\\n\\n\\n(defn encode\\n  \\\"The canonical CBOR payload bytes of one supported value (byte[] on the\\n   JVM, Uint8Array on JavaScript, Uint8List on Dart). Refuses unsupported\\n   values, unpaired surrogates, nesting deeper than max-depth, and\\n   collections whose members collide after normalization.\\\"\\n  [value]\\n  (value-bytes value 1))\\n\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.prompt.md:10:- Model: gpt-6-astra | Assigned: 2026-11-09 | Status: active\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.prompt.md:15:   — NOW SIGNED OFF by the owner (ruling of record, master 368297c3). U1:\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.prompt.md:17:   history, never minted. U2: admission identity declared by the composition\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.prompt.md:19:   distinction is declared. U3: identity never minted from structure or process.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.prompt.md:29:Does the branch's implementation of U1-U3 (a) faithfully implement the signed\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207465000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.prompt.md:10:- Model: gpt-6-astra | Assigned: 2026-11-09 | Status: active\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207465000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.prompt.md:14:Your r1 (collab/yang-clojure/1794163259000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log)\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207465000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.prompt.md:22:- The signed ruling is of record on master: 368297c3 (U1-U3).\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207465000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.prompt.md:31:   shape, which invariant (U1 read-from-history) it would violate. Quote file:line.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207465000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.prompt.md:37:   deadline waiting for response 14) compatible with U1's implementation, or does it\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794202500000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.findings.md:3:**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES — fa70516f is not merge-ready. Two P1 implementation defects remain.** This accepts signed U1–U3; it does not reopen the resolved content-address or default-admission objections.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794202500000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.findings.md:28:   **U1 violation:** the record asserts construction history that did not produce the retained application. Reading that incorrect record faithfully does not repair provenance. The same loss can occur beneath a constructor: [macro.cljc:638](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:638) also treats missing child provenance as constructed.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794170000000-architect-cc1-recheck-signed-ruling.findings.md:1:The signed ruling is present at `368297c3`, and the diff to `fa70516f` matches the stated 14 files and +2158/−116 lines. I’m tracing round 5’s construction provenance and publication custody against U1–U3.\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794207752000-engineer-cc1-p1-metadata-fixes.prompt.md:10:- Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Assigned: 2026-11-09 | Status: active | Rationale: owner relay - muse available again; muse-wonder for the macro.cljc provenance implementation (agy 429, qwen out)\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794209702000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:7:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794202500000-architect-cc1-recheck-r2.findings.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"Completed-GMT / Completed-Local: 2026-11-09 07:01 GMT / 2026-11-09 14:01 +0700\\\\n\\\\n**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES — fa70516f is not merge-ready. Two P1 implementation defects remain.** This accepts signed U1–U3; it does not reopen the resolved content-address or default-admission objections.\\\\n\\\\nAll code references below are to fa70516f. The linked cc1 files match that revision for these paths. Review was read-only; no tests were run. Reproductions below are statically traced, not executed.\\\\n\\\\n1. **P1 — Rebuilding a packet container loses retained origins and fabricates construction provenance.**\\\\n\\\\n   Reproducible source forms, compiled and expanded through the existing `expand-like-the-repl` helper:\\\\n\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\n   (defmacro repack [x]\\\\n     (conj [] (first x) (first (rest x))))\\\\n   (repack (+ 1 2))\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   `expand-call` attaches `::origin-of` to the **outer operand packet’s metadata** at [macro.cljc:1208](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1208). The prelude exposes ordinary `first`, `rest`, and `conj` through [macro.cljc:739](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:739) and [vm.cljc:398](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:398).\\\\n\\\\n   The macro returns a fresh `[root rows]` container holding the original root and rows. It constructs no application syntax, but the outer metadata disappears. Validation accepts those unchanged rows. Then [macro.cljc:1232](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1232) applies:\\\\n\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\n   (or (origin-of-fn tree)\\\\n       (fn [_] pending-expansion-origin))\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   Consequently, the output correspondence records `{[] :constructed}` instead of `{[] [:retained incoming-origin]}`. The walk translates that into `[:expansion record-address]` at [macro.cljc:1259](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1259), and the final table consumes it at [macro.cljc:1387](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1387).\\\\n\\\\n   **U1 violation:** the record asserts construction history that did not produce the retained application. Reading that incorrect record faithfully does not repair provenance. The same loss can occur beneath a constructor: [macro.cljc:638](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:638) also treats missing child provenance as constructed.\\\\n\\\\n   **Minimum correction:** preserve occurrence provenance through permitted packet decomposition/reassembly, including child insertion. Remove the assumption that missing provenance proves construction. Explicit refusal is an interim containment measure; restoring supported packet operations requires provenance propagation through those operations. Address-equality inference is not a valid replacement.\\\\n\\\\n2. **P1 — Internal provenance metadata makes an otherwise valid packet literal unencodable.**\\\\n\\\\n   Reproducible forms:\\\\n\\\\n   ```clojure\\\\n   (defmacro packet-data [x] (yin/literal x))\\\\n   (packet-data (+ 1 2))\\\\n   ```\\\\n\\\\n   [macro.cljc:618](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:618) attaches a host function as `::origin-of`. `yin/literal` passes the operand directly into `[:literal v]` at [macro.cljc:667](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:667). `construct` interns that body at [macro.cljc:655](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:655), before output validation.\\\\n\\\\n   Jing encodes vector metadata: [cbor.cljc:904](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:904) calls `meta-bytes`; [cbor.cljc:834](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:834) removes only reader-position keys, leaving `::origin-of`. Encoding its function value reaches the unsupported-value refusal. The bounded runner converts the exception into `:body-error` at [macro.cljc:829](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:829).\\\\n\\\\n   Thus internal tracking changes valid macro behavior. The claim that this metadata is “content-addressing invisible” is false when a packet becomes literal data.\\\\n\\\\n   **Minimum correction:** remove only private tracking metadata, recursively, when values enter literal/data slots, before hashing and validation; preserve legitimate user metadata. Keeping tracking entirely outside macro-visible values would also resolve this boundary problem. Do not change Jing’s metadata semantics to accommodate it.\\\\n\\\\n**These are current round-5 defects, not stale pre-fix findings.** The relevant implementation is unchanged between round-5 commit `847aa885` and fa70516f. Round 5 correctly handles direct pass-through and constructor-mediated composition, including the tested identical-content twins; it does not cover the two paths above. The reported Node and JVM results—27 tests/242 assertions each—do not contradict these uncovered cases.\\\\n\\\\n**Corpus ruling:** the signature difference is compatible with added provenance work, but does not establish its cause. Response `14` is zero-based and names `<?php echo 1 + 2;`: see [runner:94](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_shell_session.clj:94) and [fixture:8](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/resources/yin/repl/transcripts/local.edn:8). The runner gives each response 180 seconds.\\\\n\\\\nThe recorded branch timeout also occurred **in isolation**, so worker starvation is not an adequate explanation. Cc1 adds occurrence enumeration, correspondence sorting, and origin bookkeeping; these add compilation cost without inherently changing executable tree structure. The PHP prelude-depth defect explains master’s overflow, and `f4df9893` fixes that structure. **That fix is not contained in fa70516f.**\\\\n\\\\nAccordingly, I find no demonstrated third cc1 defect from the timeout alone, but “master also fails” does not fully exonerate the branch’s timing behavior. A comparison on the same PHP-fixed base would resolve that residual attribution question.\\\\n\\\\n**Final disposition: do not merge fa70516f. The two P1 metadata defects block approval independently of the corpus question. This closes the cc1 re-check with a request-changes verdict.**\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794209702000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log:17:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_7\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'git -C /tmp/cc1-p1 diff -- src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-CYAVFcqM' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\\\n2026-11-09 14:35:33.434 xcodebuild[12341:118717846]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\\\n2026-11-09 14:35:33.668 xcodebuild[12341:118717842] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\\\\\"Input/output error\\\\\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-T2XSL5se' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\\\n2026-11-09 14:35:34.613 xcodebuild[12348:118717910]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\\\\n2026-11-09 14:35:34.878 xcodebuild[12348:118717904] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \\\\\\\"Input/output error\\\\\\\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\\\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\\\\nindex 07240a92..6f2903f8 100644\\\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc\\\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yi