xpander creates metadata unconditionally); F2-residual — publish-module! ~:260 stores the table beside the manifest but the manifest does not REFERENCE it (the closure transfer loses it), and call-site-claim ~:127 checks paths but not marker VALUES (a version-2 table accepted, the retriever returns nil). (2) The rule applied honestly: two gate-failed rounds on the same model (muse) — the diversity requirement points to a different model, and the strongest context holder is kimi-k3.1-pro (its final aaq gate analyzed these exact custody surfaces). Fix round 2 dispatched to kimi-k3.1-pro as an IMPLEMENTER subagent (general-purpose, full tools, the cc1 worktree): per-load-keyed metadata + conditional creation (defect 1), manifest references carrying the table through the closure + version enforcement at call-site-claim (defect 2), four regression tests (successive expansions, no-claim batches, transport retrieval, version rejection). Boundaries: macro.cljc + linker/publish.cljc + the test file (+ minimal manifest plumbing justified); the D1 durable store stays out of scope.\\\\\\\\nDecisions: the fix round goes to a different model per the diversity requirement — kimi implements, codex re-gates (the reviewer/implementer roles stay separate).\\\\\\\\nVerification: the gate's file/line refs are the spec; the four regression tests are the acceptance.\\\\\\\\nDelegates: kimi-k3.1-pro (cc1 fix round 2 implementer, IN FLIGHT); codex (the next re-gate, queued).\\\\\\\\nNext: kimi's fix lands -> my verification -> the focused codex re-gate -> ACCEPT -> merge -> adoption rounds 2-4 + D1 -> the generalization completes.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2026-11-07 1x:xx +07 — cc1 fix round 4 (8844f96d) delivered; codex gate REJECTS on occurrence-identity semantics; mechanical round 4.1 (d91489f7) applied\\\\\\\\nDone: (1) Astra's P1 re-check on beb9cc97 rejected landing: P1-a (one origin for all retained addresses), P1-b (global counter), P2 (mixed-origin accepted) remain; the `unless` objection was withdrawn. (2) Fix round 4 dispatched to an implementer subagent: per-occurrence provenance (the admitted-origin capture deleted from expand-call; retained occurrences keep their OWN incoming provenance), scoped admission allocator (the namespace-global counter deleted; caller-owned `admission-scope` + a deterministic default token from the spec's durable identity), and multi-claim rejection with both origins in the diagnostic. 16/197/0 + oracle 31/2466/0 + kondo 0/0; pushed. (3) The codex gate: DO NOT LAND — P1-a/P1-b residuals both reduce to ONE question: occurrence identity vs content address (identical generated/input applications share an address; a deterministic default admission token makes distinct admissions of identical specs indistinguishable from a replay). Plus two mechanical findings: scope ids lose keyword namespaces (:a/publisher ≡ :b/publisher), and the default validator mode rejects a second claim as nonexistent-path instead of the multi-claim diagnostic. (4) Round 4.1 applied BY THE SEAT (d91489f7): pr-str scope ids (full identity kept), the one-origin-per-occurrence rule now enforced in EVERY validator mode with the same diagnostic, two regression tests added (17/200/0; kondo 0/0); pushed. (5) The exception-track r0 kit landed on master (0fa3ff7a, steward note 1795200000000) — R3 dispatch precondition met, still sequenced behind cc1 landing.\\\\\\\\nDecision pending THE OWNER: the occurrence-identity ruling — per-occurrence provenance for identical subtrees requires either (a) composition-supplied durable admission identities (the composition asserts which admissions are distinct events), or (b) admission-minted occurrence identity (admission-time token distinguishes otherwise-identical occurrences). In a content-addressed store identical content IS one address (unitarity) — whether \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"two occurrences of identical content\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is meaningful, and who decides distinctness, is the owner's call. My recommendation: (a) — it keeps the unitarity axiom (identity never minted from structure) and puts distinctness where the knowledge is (the composition).\\\\\\\\nDelegates: oracle full run (background); shiva remote battery at d91489f7 (background).\\\\\\\\nNext: both green + the owner's allocator ruling → the design-level fix → astra re-check → codex gate → land → R3 dispatch → adoption rounds 2-4 + D1.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n19:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_8\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git log -12 --oneline fa70516f; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git show --stat 847aa885; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --stat 368297c3...fa70516f'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"fa70516f Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/master' into cc1-rebased\\\\\\\\n368297c3 docs(yang-clojure): the occurrence-identity ruling is SIGNED OFF — ruling of record; the codex cc1 reject is answered\\\\\\\\necc4a651 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/master' into cc1-rebased\\\\\\\\nd454378b fix(dao.host): the H3 gate-census re-record — counts 175/163/161/159/152, list-1 73 -> 72\\\\\\\\nae793ec4 docs(yang-clojure): RED 2 attribution closed — the yin.repl shell-session red fails identically on clean master (StackOverflowError on shiva), pre-existing; both wide-lane reds are outside cc1\\\\\\\\n94fc5ca2 docs(yang-clojure): the cc1 findings package for reassignment — the dao.host census red (pre-existing on master, 50 vs 33 measured), the yin.repl deadline red (isolation run pending), the lane state, and the operational notes\\\\\\\\n847aa885 fix(yang.clojure): construction-threaded occurrence origins from retained expansion history (cc1 fix round 5, ruling U1)\\\\\\\\nd8afa459 docs(exception-track): the ts/php ordering ack — the prelude branch ownership registered after the custody correction; the surfaces-stay-disjoint confirmation\\\\\\\\ne251dc3d docs(exception-track): reply to the steward — the pause acknowledged; cc1 NOT landed (the codex occurrence-identity reject stands; the owner ruling pending); R3 holds per the sequencing of record\\\\\\\\nc10ded19 docs(collab): the nightly-reds-fix dispatch log completed — the round's final verification output appended after the initial filing\\\\\\\\n23f7ccc9 docs(logs): the cc1 fix rounds 4/4.1 arc — the codex occurrence-identity reject, the seat-applied mechanical fixes, the verification census, the pending owner ruling\\\\\\\\n1cc519b3 docs(archive): master-green recovery seat — collaboration artifacts and session log\\\\\\\\ncommit 847aa8856ca85a88eb3053361d62d32cd978b110\\\\\\\\nAuthor: Sonny To <son.c.to@gmail.com>\\\\\\\\nDate:   Sun Nov 8 23:11:11 2026 +0700\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    fix(yang.clojure): construction-threaded occurrence origins from retained expansion history (cc1 fix round 5, ruling U1)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc           | 204 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\\\\\\\\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc |  63 +++++++++++\\\\\\\\n 2 files changed, 223 insertions(+), 44 deletions(-)\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc           |  253 +++++++-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc   |    5 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc         |    7 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc         |   46 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc     |   16 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc                 |   14 +\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc         |  129 +++-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc          |   17 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc  |   46 +-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc  |  305 +++++++++-\\\\\\\\n src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc           |  353 +++++++++--\\\\\\\\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 1067 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\\\\\\\n test/yang/core/call_test.cljc        |    9 +-\\\\\\\\n test/yin/vm/encoder_test.cljc        |    7 +-\\\\\\\\n 14 files changed, 2158 insertions(+), 116 deletions(-)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n21:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_9\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff 368297c3...fa70516f -- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc'\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"diff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\\\\\\\\nindex 8900fd54..44aacf0e 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\\\\\\\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\\\\\\\\n@@ -738,11 +738,11 @@\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n (def ^:private manifest-keys\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The closed key set of a schema-1 manifest: every key of section 8.1's\\\\\\\\n-   example, the index alone optional.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+   example, the index and the call-site reference alone optional.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   #{:yin.module/name :yin.module/schema :yin.module/contracts\\\\\\\\n     :yin.module/tree :yin.module/derivations :yin.module/index\\\\\\\\n     :yin.module/exports :yin.module/requires :yin.module/primitives\\\\\\\\n-    :yin.module/footprint})\\\\\\\\n+    :yin.module/footprint :yin.module/call-sites})\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n (def ^:private derivation-formats\\\\\\\\n@@ -785,7 +785,8 @@\\\\\\\\n                   (when (or (not (contains? manifest k))\\\\\\\\n                             (nil? (get manifest k)))\\\\\\\\n                     (assoc (shape k) :missing true)))\\\\\\\\n-                (disj manifest-keys :yin.module/index))\\\\\\\\n+                (disj manifest-keys :yin.module/index\\\\\\\\n+                      :yin.module/call-sites))\\\\\\\\n           (when-not (symbol? (:yin.module/name manifest))\\\\\\\\n             (shape :yin.module/name))\\\\\\\\n           (when (vm/reserved-name? (:yin.module/name manifest))\\\\\\\\n@@ -831,6 +832,16 @@\\\\\\\\n                          (set? (get-in manifest\\\\\\\\n                                        [:yin.module/footprint :effects])))\\\\\\\\n             (shape :yin.module/footprint))\\\\\\\\n+          ;; optional, and only when present checked: the C1 side-table\\\\\\\\n+          ;; reference is exactly the table's and the reverse record's\\\\\\\\n+          ;; Jing addresses (`yin.vm.linker.publish`)\\\\\\\\n+          (let [call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\\\\\\\\n+            (when (and (some? call-sites)\\\\\\\\n+                       (not (and (map? call-sites)\\\\\\\\n+                                 (= #{:table :record} (set (keys call-sites)))\\\\\\\\n+                                 (address? (:table call-sites))\\\\\\\\n+                                 (address? (:record call-sites)))))\\\\\\\\n+              (shape :yin.module/call-sites)))\\\\\\\\n           (some (fn [n]\\\\\\\\n                   (when (vm/reserved-name? n)\\\\\\\\n                     {:rule :reserved-name, :name n,\\\\\\\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\\\\\\\\nindex 3b99b7ea..bfb8168e 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\\\\\\\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\\\\\\\\n@@ -192,6 +192,43 @@\\\\\\\\n (declare walk-module)\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n+(defn- walk-call-sites\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Step 4b: the C1 side table and its reverse record the manifest\\\\\\\\n+   references (`:yin.module/call-sites`, `yin.vm.linker.publish`), read\\\\\\\\n+   and held to their own shape — the table is a vector of frontend-\\\\\\\\n+   metadata rows, the record is version 1, names the manifest's own\\\\\\\\n+   tree, and points at the referenced table. The origin is not\\\\\\\\n+   recomputed or reconstructed here: each marker row carries its own\\\\\\\\n+   occurrence origin (design §2.1), and the record persists the\\\\\\\\n+   publication's admission identity, which the retriever reads from\\\\\\\\n+   the record, never from the tree.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [st manifest path]\\\\\\\\n+  (if-some [call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\\\\\\\\n+    (let [[st table] (read-blob st (:table call-sites) :call-site path)]\\\\\\\\n+      (if (:stop st)\\\\\\\\n+        st\\\\\\\\n+        (let [[st record] (read-blob st (:record call-sites) :call-site path)]\\\\\\\\n+          (cond\\\\\\\\n+            (:stop st) st\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+            (not (vector? table))\\\\\\\\n+            (stop st (invalid (:table call-sites) :call-site path\\\\\\\\n+                              :call-site-defect {:code :table-shape}))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+            (not= {:yang.call-site/version 1\\\\\\\\n+                   :yang.call-site/root (:yin.module/tree manifest)\\\\\\\\n+                   :yang.call-site/table (:table call-sites)}\\\\\\\\n+                  (select-keys record\\\\\\\\n+                               [:yang.call-site/version\\\\\\\\n+                                :yang.call-site/root\\\\\\\\n+                                :yang.call-site/table]))\\\\\\\\n+            (stop st (invalid (:record call-sites) :call-site path\\\\\\\\n+                              :call-site-defect {:code :record-shape}))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+            :else st))))\\\\\\\\n+    st))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n (defn- walk-requires\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Step 5: list every pin with derived eagerness, then descend only into\\\\\\\\n    eager manifests not walked before. Deferred pins load at statement time.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n@@ -242,7 +279,8 @@\\\\\\\\n                    (update :modules conj manifest-address)\\\\\\\\n                    (walk-rows (:yin.module/tree manifest) path))\\\\\\\\n             st (if (:stop st) st (walk-records st manifest path))\\\\\\\\n-            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-images st manifest path))]\\\\\\\\n+            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-images st manifest path))\\\\\\\\n+            st (if (:stop st) st (walk-call-sites st manifest path))]\\\\\\\\n         (if (:stop st)\\\\\\\\n           st\\\\\\\\n           (walk-requires st manifest-address manifest path depth))))))\\\\\\\\n@@ -262,11 +300,13 @@\\\\\\\\n      {:yin.link.closure/outcome :invalid\\\\\\\\n       :address a :role role :path [...] :defect {:code c :detail d}}\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n-   `role` is `:manifest`, `:row`, `:record`, `:image` or `:require`;\\\\\\\\n+   `role` is `:manifest`, `:row`, `:record`, `:image`, `:call-site` or\\\\\\\\n+   `:require`;\\\\\\\\n    `path` the manifest addresses from the root to the module the blob\\\\\\\\n    belongs to.  `:code` is one of `:address-mismatch`, `:manifest-defect`,\\\\\\\\n    `:row-defect`, `:record-defect`, `:derivation-mismatch`,\\\\\\\\n-   `:index-entry-missing`, `:identity-mismatch`, `:parts-limit`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+   `:index-entry-missing`, `:identity-mismatch`, `:call-site-defect`,\\\\\\\\n+   `:parts-limit`.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   ([handle manifest-address] (walk handle manifest-address nil))\\\\\\\\n   ([handle manifest-address opts]\\\\\\\\n    (let [bounds (into linker/default-bounds\\\\\\\\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\\\\\\\\nindex c5dc7161..f706f033 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\\\\\\\\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\\\\\\\\n@@ -90,6 +90,131 @@\\\\\\\\n    linker/stack-format linker/register-format])\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n+;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\\\\\\\\n+;; =============================================================================\\\\\\\\n+;;\\\\\\\\n+;; A module whose frontend finalized its tree (`:yang/call-site 1` on\\\\\\\\n+;; every final `:application` occurrence) publishes its frontend-metadata\\\\\\\\n+;; side table with its manifest: the manifest keeps schema 1 (a manifest\\\\\\\\n+;; address names code) and gains the optional `:yin.module/call-sites`\\\\\\\\n+;; reference `{table record}` — the module closure follows manifest\\\\\\\\n+;; references, so only a referenced table travels with the module\\\\\\\\n+;; through transfer. The reverse record names the tree root, the\\\\\\\\n+;; publication's recorded admission origin, and the table's address; it\\\\\\\\n+;; cannot name the manifest (the manifest references it, so the two\\\\\\\\n+;; addresses would be circular), and custody runs one way, from the\\\\\\\\n+;; manifest forward. The publication's origin is an ADMISSION identity\\\\\\\\n+;; (design §2.1): a token the composition pins explicitly, draws from\\\\\\\\n+;; a composition-owned scope object, or — by default — has derived\\\\\\\\n+;; from the publication specification's own durable identity; no\\\\\\\\n+;; counter or other mutable state lives in this namespace. The token\\\\\\\\n+;; is persisted in the record and retrieved from the record, never\\\\\\\\n+;; reconstructed from the tree's content. The publisher\\\\\\\\n+;; extracts the markers from the map AST, refuses the\\\\\\\\n+;; publication when they do not exactly cover the canonical tree's\\\\\\\\n+;; application occurrences — or when a marker's value is not version 1 —\\\\\\\\n+;; and otherwise materializes the table and its record into the same\\\\\\\\n+;; handle. A module with no markers makes no claim and publishes exactly\\\\\\\\n+;; as before.\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn admission-scope\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"An admission scope for `publish-module!`'s `:yin.link.publish/scope`\\\\\\\\n+   option. `id` names this publisher — a durable, caller-chosen\\\\\\\\n+   identity (a string or keyword) that distinguishes this publisher's\\\\\\\\n+   admissions from every other publisher's; a publisher that must not\\\\\\\\n+   collide with its own past runs takes a fresh `id` per run. The\\\\\\\\n+   returned scope object OWNS the publication ordinal counter, so no\\\\\\\\n+   counter lives in this namespace (no hidden global state): two\\\\\\\\n+   publications through one scope draw consecutive ordinals, and two\\\\\\\\n+   independent scopes publishing identical specifications still yield\\\\\\\\n+   distinct admission identities, because their `id`s differ.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [id]\\\\\\\\n+  {:yin.link.publish/scope-id id\\\\\\\\n+   :yin.link.publish/ordinal (atom 0)})\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn- scope-admission-token\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The admission token a scope object draws for one publication: the\\\\\\\\n+   scope's own `id` plus the ordinal the scope's counter assigns. The\\\\\\\\n+   counter lives in the caller-owned scope object, never here.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [{:yin.link.publish/keys [scope-id ordinal]}]\\\\\\\\n+  ;; pr-str keeps the value's full identity — a keyword's namespace, a\\\\\\\\n+  ;; string's quoting, a symbol's name — so distinct caller-chosen ids\\\\\\\\n+  ;; (:a/publisher, :b/publisher, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"publisher\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\") never mint the same token\\\\\\\\n+  (keyword \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"yin.vm.linker.publish.scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+           (str (pr-str scope-id) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"#\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (swap! ordinal inc))))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn- spec-admission-token\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The default admission token: derived deterministically from the\\\\\\\\n+   publication specification's own durable identity — the module name\\\\\\\\n+   and the content address of its compiled tree — never from hidden\\\\\\\\n+   mutable state. Two publications of the same specification therefore\\\\\\\\n+   answer the same admission identity (an idempotent re-publication is\\\\\\\\n+   the same recorded admission), and distinct specifications never\\\\\\\\n+   share one, in this or any other publisher process. A composition\\\\\\\\n+   that admits the same specification more than once as separate\\\\\\\\n+   admissions passes an `:yin.link.publish/scope` (or an explicit\\\\\\\\n+   `:yin.link.publish/admission`) so the admissions stay distinct.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [{:keys [name]} tree]\\\\\\\\n+  (keyword \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"yin.vm.linker.publish.publication\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+           (str name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"::\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" (:root tree))))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn- publication-origin\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The occurrence origin of the publication admission `token` names:\\\\\\\\n+   the publisher's own medium, the explicit admission token, member 0.\\\\\\\\n+   `token` is the publication's admission identity — the\\\\\\\\n+   `:yin.link.publish/admission` option when the composition pins one,\\\\\\\\n+   the `:yin.link.publish/scope` option's next drawn token when the\\\\\\\\n+   composition scopes the publisher, otherwise the token derived from\\\\\\\\n+   the publication specification's own durable identity. The origin is\\\\\\\\n+   an admission event's identity, not a function of the tree's content\\\\\\\\n+   alone: it is persisted in the side record at publication time and\\\\\\\\n+   retrieved from that record; nothing ever reconstructs it from the\\\\\\\\n+   root.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [token]\\\\\\\\n+  [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0])\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn- claims-call-sites?\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 key anywhere. A hit inside a\\\\\\\\n+   literal payload is data, not a claim: extraction then finds no\\\\\\\\n+   markers and the module publishes unannotated, as it should.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [ast]\\\\\\\\n+  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+(defn- call-site-claim\\\\\\\\n+  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The C1 claim `ast` makes over its canonical `tree`: nil when it\\\\\\\\n+   carries no markers; `{:origin o :rows [...]}` in printed-row order\\\\\\\\n+   when the extracted markers exactly cover the tree's eligible\\\\\\\\n+   application occurrences; `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` when they\\\\\\\\n+   do not; `{:unsupported-version v :path p}` when a marker's value is\\\\\\\\n+   not version 1 — a claim rejection, never a silent acceptance of a\\\\\\\\n+   table a retriever would read as version 1.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+  [ast tree admission]\\\\\\\\n+  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\\\\\\\\n+    (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\\\\\\\\n+          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\\\\\\\\n+                            (:frontend-metadata\\\\\\\\n+                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\\\\\\\\n+          eligible (into #{}\\\\\\\\n+                         (map (fn [[r p]] [origin r p]))\\\\\\\\n+                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))\\\\\\\\n+          marked (into #{}\\\\\\\\n+                       (map (fn [[o r p _ _]] [o r p]))\\\\\\\\n+                       extracted)]\\\\\\\\n+      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\\\\\\\\n+                                   (let [v (nth row 4)]\\\\\\\\n+                                     (when (not (and (integer? v) (= 1 v)))\\\\\\\\n+                                       [v (subvec row 0 3)])))\\\\\\\\n+                                 extracted)]\\\\\\\\n+            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\\\\\\\\n+          (if (= eligible marked)\\\\\\\\n+            {:origin origin, :rows (vec (sort-by pr-str extracted))}\\\\\\\\n+            {:missing (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove marked eligible))),\\\\\\\\n+             :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove eligible marked)))})))))\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n (defn link-local\\\\\\\\n   \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Link `format`'s image through the manifest `address` over `handle`'s\\\\\\\\n    own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\\\\\\\\n@@ -138,7 +263,25 @@\\\\\\\\n                 (sort-by (fn [[n _]] (str n)) requires)))\\\\\\\\n         fp (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\\\\\\\\n                       (not= :refused (:status tree)))\\\\\\\\n-             (footprint handle (assoc spec :tree tree)))]\\\\\\\\n+             (footprint handle (assoc spec :tree tree)))\\\\\\\\n+        ;; a C1 claim is validated before anything is written: a module\\\\\\\\n+        ;; whose markers do not cover its tree is never published as\\\\\\\\n+        ;; though it did. One publication is one admission event\\\\\\\\n+        ;; (design §2.1): the admission identity is pinned explicitly by\\\\\\\\n+        ;; the composition when it supplies `:yin.link.publish/admission`,\\\\\\\\n+        ;; drawn from the composition's own scope object when it supplies\\\\\\\\n+        ;; `:yin.link.publish/scope`, and otherwise derived from the\\\\\\\\n+        ;; specification's own durable identity — no counter lives in\\\\\\\\n+        ;; this namespace. Either way it is persisted in the side record\\\\\\\\n+        ;; and retrieved from there\\\\\\\\n+        admission (or (:yin.link.publish/admission opts)\\\\\\\\n+                      (when-let [scope (:yin.link.publish/scope opts)]\\\\\\\\n+                        (scope-admission-token scope))\\\\\\\\n+                      (when tree (spec-admission-token spec tree)))\\\\\\\\n+        claim (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\\\\\\\\n+                         (not= :refused (:status tree))\\\\\\\\n+                         (not= :refused (:status fp)))\\\\\\\\n+                (call-site-claim ast tree admission))]\\\\\\\\n     (cond\\\\\\\\n       undefined\\\\\\\\n       (refusal :yin.link.publish/undefined-export {:export undefined})\\\\\\\\n@@ -152,6 +295,16 @@\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n       (= :refused (:status fp)) fp\\\\\\\\n \\\\\\\\n+      ;; dispatch on the key's PRESENCE, not