ault and only mode. A recursion-depth bound\\\\n  1927\\\\t  is available if a composition wants one (PHP has none; default off).\\\\n  1928\\\\t- `max_execution_time` and `set_time_limit` are wall-clock in PHP and so\\\\n  1929\\\\t  nondeterministic: the profile offers a deterministic **safepoint-count\\\\n  1930\\\\t  budget** instead, raising the fatal with PHP's text, a recorded departure\\\\n  1931\\\\t  (owner decision B8.5, corner C21). A composition may supply one non-negative\\\\n  1932\\\\t  integer budget per run; omission means unlimited. Each entry to a `:loop` or\\\\n  1933\\\\t  `:call` hook consumes one unit, and the hook after the last available unit\\\\n  1934\\\\t  raises `PHP Fatal error:  Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded`.\\\\n  1935\\\\t  This operational fatal is not guest-catchable and skips shutdown functions\\\\n  1936\\\\t  and destructors. It bounds execution between hooks, not wall-clock time or\\\\n  1937\\\\t  blocking host operations; no generic VM instructions are charged.\\\\n  1938\\\\t- **Statement ticks** (`declare(ticks=N)`, `register_tick_function`) need\\\\n  1939\\\\t  `:line` sites before non-lambda statement nodes. `yang.safepoint` currently\\\\n  1940\\\\t  refuses a selected site that is not a `:lambda` (`site-not-lambda`), and\\\\n  1941\\\\t  `:line` insertion is safepoint slice 3, which Python tracing also needs.\\\\n  1942\\\\t  Ticks therefore **depend on the shared `:line` extension**: P7 splits into\\\\n  1943\\\\t  P7-a (signals, no dependency) and P7-b (ticks, behind safepoint slice 3).\\\\n  1944\\\\t  Neither L1 to L4 nor this frontend extends `yang.safepoint`; the extension\\\\n  1945\\\\t  is the safepoint seat's.\\\\n  1946\\\\t- No thread switches: PHP is single-threaded, and one request is one task.\\\\n  1947\\\\t\\\\n  1948\\\\t## 13. Diagnostics\\\\n  1949\\\\t\\\\n  1950\\\\tCompile time: `:yang.php/syntax`; `:yang.php/unsupported {:construct}`;\\\\n  1951\\\\t`:yang.php/not-php`; `:yang.php/unknown-builtin` (a warning);\\\\n  1952\\\\t`:yang.php/compile-error` for PHP's compile-time fatals (a function redeclared\\\\n  1953\\\\tin one unit, `break 0`, a duplicate parameter, `$this` reassignment, a\\\\n  1954\\\\tpositional argument after a named one). Run time: guest warnings, notices and\\\\n  1955\\\\tdeprecations as records on the guest-diagnostics stream; fatals as `Error`\\\\n  1956\\\\tthrows; the uncaught-exception text pinned. Operational failures stay\\\\n  1957\\\\toperational (`yang.antlr.md` section 11).\\\\n  1958\\\\t\\\\n  1959\\\\t## 14. The differential-corpus plan\\\\n  1960\\\\t\\\\n  1961\\\\t- **Oracle**: the pinned PHP 8.3.x CLI with the pinned ini. The comparison\\\\n  1962\\\\t  covers stdout and the diagnostics stream, rendered in PHP's `Warning: ... in\\\\n  1963\\\\t  <unit> on line N` form with the path replaced by the unit name and the line\\\\n  1964\\\\t  derived from the side table (owner decision 2 of `yang.antlr.md` 8.5.1\\\\n  1965\\\\t  reused), against PHP's stderr with paths normalized.\\\\n  1966\\\\t- **Groups**: juggling (every pair of the comparison matrix, numeric strings,\\\\n  1967\\\\t  arithmetic warnings and `TypeError`); arrays (key coercion, order, next\\\\n  1968\\\\t  index after unset, copy-on-write observable through references, nested\\\\n  1969\\\\t  writes, sort stability); references and lifecycle (section 4.6's three\\\\n  1970\\\\t  sources); strings (bytes, interpolation forms, heredoc indentation,\\\\n  2090\\\\t|       | `use`, constants, the autoload   | imports on Node and Dart with     |\\\\n  2091\\\\t|       | class map, publication and DHT   | equal output; the computed-path   |\\\\n  2092\\\\t|       | import parserless on Node and    | diagnostic; an unpublished target |\\\\n  2093\\\\t|       | Dart, the dynamic-scope profile  | refused at publication by name; a |\\\\n  2094\\\\t|       | for including functions          | pinned but unserved target:       |\\\\n  2095\\\\t|       |                                  | `include` warns and yields        |\\\\n  2096\\\\t|       |                                  | `false`, `require` and            |\\\\n  2097\\\\t|       |                                  | `require_once` throw `Error`; a   |\\\\n  2098\\\\t|       |                                  | refused `_once` retries delivery  |\\\\n  2099\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2100\\\\t| P7-a  | signals: `phpsp` hooks at        | a signal at a `:loop` hook runs   |\\\\n  2101\\\\t|       | `:loop` and `:call`,             | the handler; an empty signal      |\\\\n  2102\\\\t|       | `pcntl_signal`, the safepoint    | stream never parks; budget        |\\\\n  2103\\\\t|       | budget                           | exhaustion raises the pinned      |\\\\n  2104\\\\t|       |                                  | fatal text                        |\\\\n  2105\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2106\\\\t| P7-b  | ticks: `declare(ticks)`,         | tick counts equal PHP's for the   |\\\\n  2107\\\\t|       | `register_tick_function`; behind | statement fixture                 |\\\\n  2108\\\\t|       | safepoint slice 3                |                                   |\\\\n  2109\\\\t+-------+----------------------------------+-----------------------------------+\\\\n  2110\\\\t| P8    | legacy retirement: the legacy    | the REPL prints `1` for `<?php $x |\\\\n  2111\\\\t|       | test programs in the new corpus, | = 1; echo $x;`; every legacy test |\\\\n  2112\\\\t|       | the demo on checked-in CST       | program passes with corrected     |\\\\n  2113\\\\t|       | packets,                         | expectations; the demo runs its   |\\\\n  2114\\\\t|       | `src/dev/subsystems.edn`         | samples parserless in the         |\\\\n  2115\\\\t|       | retargeted, `yang/php.cljc`      | browser; no reference to the      |\\\\n