re:| departure        |\\\\n  2430\\\\t|                     | the call is refused as              | `G-default-      |\\\\n  2431\\\\t|                     | `G-default-autoload`; Composer      | autoload`; class |\\\\n  2432\\\\t|                     | class-map data is allowed, its      | map data remains |\\\\n  2433\\\\t|                     | filesystem lookup is not.           | supported        |\\\\n  2434\\\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\n  2435\\\\t\\\\n  2436\\\\t### 17.3 Convergence and the blocking rule\\\\n  2437\\\\t\\\\n  2438\\\\t**Claimed rows are normative, and a known-incorrect claimed row blocks.** A\\\\n  2439\\\\trow of the transition table is a statement of Zend's behaviour, fixed from the\\\\n  2440\\\\thandler source and **confirmed by the oracle before the slice that claims it\\\\n  2441\\\\tlands**. After landing, a disagreement between a row and the pinned PHP CLI is\\\\n  2442\\\\ta defect of the row, never of the fixture. A finding that a claimed row\\\\n  2443\\\\tcontradicts Zend blocks landing of any slice whose support profile includes\\\\n  2444\\\\tthat row until either the row is corrected (and its fixture regenerated from\\\\n  2445\\\\tthe oracle), or the Architect explicitly moves the behaviour to section 17.2\\\\n  2446\\\\tas a restricted corner with a departure fixture whose expected value is the\\\\n  2447\\\\trecorded deviation, with the owner's acceptance when the corner touches a\\\\n  2448\\\\tPhase 3 exit criterion. Regenerating a fixture to match an incorrect row is\\\\n  2449\\\\tforbidden: oracle fixtures pin behaviour; they do not legitimize a\\\\n  2450\\\\tcontradictory normative rule.\\\\n  2451\\\\t\\\\n  2452\\\\tThe landing gate is therefore: every claimed-row fixture equals the oracle;\\\\n  2453\\\\tevery corner's departure fixture equals its recorded deviation; no fixture\\\\n  2454\\\\tfailure is unclassified. A new finding lands in one of four bins, in blocking\\\\n  2455\\\\torder:\\\\n  2456\\\\t\\\\n  2457\\\\t1. a defect in a claimed row (blocks);\\\\n  2458\\\\t2. a missing row required by an exit criterion or the C4 profile (blocks);\\\\n  2459\\\\t3. a reclassification request, row to corner (an Architect decision recorded\\\\n  2460\\\\t   in the ledger; blocks until decided);\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.6|eval|JVM|parse|compiler' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'php|source|JVM' src/cljc/yang/stage.cljc; rg --files src | rg 'yang/.+(parse|stage)|php'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.6|eval|JVM|parse|compiler' docs/design/yang.antlr.md; rg -n 'php|source|JVM' src/cljc/yang/stage.cljc; rg --files src | rg 'yang/.+(parse|stage)|php'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"8:pilot pipeline (parser stage, scope analysis, lowering, prelude;\\\\n40:8.11, and add cross-references from sections 8.6 and 8.9. Landed on\\\\n100:are compiled, through ANTLR-generated parsers hosted behind a stream\\\\n104:The architectural decision is to make Yang an **open compiler composition\\\\n111:ANTLR operates behind a stream boundary. Its generated parsers and\\\\n118:Remote compiler and content services use `dao.stream.remote` mirror and\\\\n140:Host parser interpreter / isolated ANTLR worker\\\\n167:The direct evaluator route and the macro route are composition\\\\n168:alternatives. A composition must not feed both into one evaluator and\\\\n195:  (`src/cljc/yang/php.cljc`) contain handwritten tokenizers, parsers, and\\\\n208:  unsuccessful appends;