c/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc:389:  (into [['php/include-path include-path-text]] module-forms))\\\\nnl: test/yang/php/antlr/harness.cljc: No such file or directory\\\\n   850\\\\tcompiler-step(stream-handles, state, work-budget)\\\\n   851\\\\t  -> {:yang.compile/state ...\\\\n   852\\\\t      :yang.compile/status ...\\\\n   853\\\\t      :yang.compile/progress ...}\\\\n   854\\\\t```\\\\n   855\\\\t\\\\n   856\\\\tHandles stay in host-local composition. Portable state carries\\\\n   857\\\\tidentities and descriptors where needed; it does not serialize handles.\\\\n   858\\\\t\\\\n   859\\\\tBudgets cover reads, transitions, writes, and work on large structures.\\\\n   860\\\\tExisting synchronous encoding, hashing, validation, or query helpers\\\\n   861\\\\tmust be made stepped or run in workers when their input can be large.\\\\n   862\\\\tAdding a `budget` argument around an unbounded recursive function is\\\\n   863\\\\tinsufficient.\\\\n   864\\\\t\\\\n   865\\\\tThe caller drives steps. Cadence or `dao.stream.waitset` can reduce idle\\\\n   866\\\\tpolling, but no interpreter requires a readiness extension.\\\\n   867\\\\t\\\\n   868\\\\tA compilation request is itself an effect descriptor appended by\\\\n   869\\\\tportable code: it names the source unit revision, the frontend revision\\\\n   870\\\\tand dialect, and the options, and it carries a request identity. The\\\\n   871\\\\tcompiler coordinator consumes those descriptors and appends outcomes.\\\\n   872\\\\tPortable code never calls the compiler as a function.\\\\n   873\\\\t\\\\n   874\\\\t### 6.2 Respect the existing outcome algebra\\\\n   875\\\\t\\\\n   876\\\\tCompiler outcomes and DaoStream outcomes occupy different layers:\\\\n   877\\\\t\\\\n   878\\\\t```clojure\\\\n   879\\\\t;; Successful observation of a failed compilation.\\\\n   880\\\\t{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\\\\n   881\\\\t :dao.stream/value\\\\n   882\\\\t {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\\\\n   883\\\\t  :yang.compile/request [\\\\\\\"client-token\\\\\\\" 12]\\\\n   884\\\\t  :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/syntax-error}\\\\n   885\\\\t :dao.stream/cursor successor}\\\\n   886\\\\t```\\\\n   887\\\\t\\\\n   888\\\\tDo not invent `:dao.stream/syntax-error` or extend DaoStream's seven\\\\n   889\\\\toperations.\\\\n   890\\\\t\\\\n  3416\\\\t### 8.6 Object-oriented and web: PHP, mixed text and ordered maps\\\\n  3417\\\\t\\\\n  3418\\\\tThe lexer uses modes to preserve HTML/text and PHP regions in source\\\\n  3419\\\\torder. Text outside code lowers to ordered output effects; it is not\\\\n  3420\\\\tdiscarded by stripping tags.\\\\n  3421\\\\t\\\\n  3422\\\\tPHP arrays require ordered-map behavior, including key conversion and\\\\n  3423\\\\titeration rules. A plain host hash map is not a sufficient\\\\n  3424\\\\trepresentation.\\\\n  3425\\\\t\\\\n  3426\\\\tThe semantic profile must cover:\\\\n  3427\\\\t\\\\n  3428\\\\t- `$var` binding and function/global/static scope.\\\\n  3429\\\\t- Capture by value versus capture by reference.\\\\n  3430\\\\t- References and aliasing.\\\\n  3431\\\\t- Ordered arrays and observable copy behavior.\\\\n  3432\\\\t- Coercion, comparisons, missing values, and error behavior.\\\\n  3433\\\\t- Function and class calls, including supported type declarations.\\\\n  3434\\\\t\\\\n  3435\\\\tSection 8.11 maps PHP arrays, objects, and references onto cells.\\\\n  3436\\\\t\\\\n  3437\\\\tSuperglobals are explicit request-context values supplied by the\\\\n  3438\\\\tcomposition. They do not read ambient process or HTTP state.\\\\n  3439\\\\t\\\\n  3440\\\\t`include` and `require` perform module-resolution effects with recorded\\\\n  3441\\\\tinputs. `eval` is a new compilation request, subject to the same\\\\n  3442\\\\tprofiles and diagnostics.\\\\n  3443\\\\t\\\\n  3444\\\\tThe existing frontend's ignored type hints and limited closure handling\\\\n  3445\\\\tare migration limitations, not semantics to preserve as the new default.\\\\n  3446\\\\t\\\\n  3447\\\\t### 8.7 Prototype: JavaScript, lexical environments and jobs\\\\n  3448\\\\t\\\\n  3449\\\\tThe frontend distinguishes script and module goals and pins an\\\\n  3450\\\\tECMAScript edition.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"web_search\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"exec-92c29eac-57ed-4dc2-8bbd-58f8d7c91a6e\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"action\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"other\\\"}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"web_search\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"exec-92c29eac-57ed-4dc2-8bbd-58f8d7c91a6e\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.eval.php\\\",\\\"action\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"open_page\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.eval.php\\\"},\\\"results\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text_result\\\",\\\"domain\\\":\\\"www.php.net\\\",\\\"ref_id\\\":\\\"turn0view0\\\",\\\"snippet\\\":\\\"Total lines: 398\\\",\\\"thumbnail_url\\\":\\\"https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-1/NZ4RoqlMbjOSQ65J5CulC0u_0Lnd6vthibR9T61-5haxMZzaHHczkhG9GlyzRzl31c8gMjgjr1zn7A-acFGFrA\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"PHP: eval - Manual\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.eval.php\\\"}]}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc | sed -n '1,260p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude_module.cljc | sed -n '1,260p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"     1\\\\t(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.php.antlr.quoted/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\\\\n     2\\\\t yang.php.antlr.prelude-module\\\\n     3\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The include/require runtime of the PHP profile (docs/design/yang.php.md\\\\n     4\\\\t   section 11, plan P6 R3/R4): the four kinds, the `_once` check, the two\\\\n     5\\\\t   missing stages. Guest code like the rest of the prelude; the lowering\\\\n     6\\\\t   emits only applications of these names.\\\\n     7\\\\t\\\\n     8\\\\t   Runtime state `php/init!` allocates for it (prelude.cljc owns the keys):\\\\n     9\\\\t     php.rt/included   a cell, map of normalized path to true; written on\\\\n    10\\\\t                       `:ok` delivery only, never on a refusal\\\\n    11\\\\t     php.rt/unit       a cell, the executing unit's path or :php/null\\\\n    12\\\\t     php.rt/path-map   a cell, map of normalized path to a delivery thunk\\\\n    13\\\\t                       (the literal path map of the composition's `:paths`)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    14\\\\t  (:require\\\\n    15\\\\t    #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn])\\\\n    16\\\\t    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]))\\\\n    17\\\\t\\\\n    18\\\\t\\\\n    19\\\\t(def include-path-text\\\\n    20\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The `include_path` the missing-include texts print: the oracle image's\\\\n    21\\\\t   default. PENDING the S0 oracle pin (php:8.3-cli reports\\\\n    22\\\\t   `.:/usr/local/lib/php`).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    23\\\\t  \\\\\\\".:/usr/local/lib/php\\\\\\\")\\\\n    24\\\\t\\\\n    25\\\\t\\\\n    26\\\\t(def include-kinds\\\\n    27\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The four kinds the lowering passes to `php/include-run`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    28\\\\t  #{:include :include-once :require :require-once})\\\\n    29\\\\t\\\\n    30\\\\t\\\\n    31\\\\t(defquoted ^:private module-forms\\\\n    32\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The include definitions, `[store-key form]`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    33\\\\t  '[[php/include-kind-name\\\\n    34\\\\t     (fn [kind]\\\\n    35\\\\t       (if (= kind :include)\\\\n    36\\\\t         \\\\\\\"include\\\\\\\"\\\\n    37\\\\t         (if (= kind :include-once)\\\\n    38\\\\t           \\\\\\\"include_once\\\\\\\"\\\\n    39\\\\t           (if (= kind :require) \\\\\\\"require\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"require_once\\\\\\\"))))]\\\\n    40\\\\t    [php/include-require?\\\\n    41\\\\t     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :require) true (= kind :require-once)))]\\\\n    42\\\\t    [php/include-once?\\\\n    43\\\\t     (fn [kind] (if (= kind :include-once) true (= kind :require-once)))]\\\\n    44\\\\t    [php/warn-refusal\\\\n    45\\\\t     ;; php/warn with the structured refusal on the record (plan R4)\\\\n    46\\\\t     (fn [errno msg refusal]\\\\n    47\\\\t       (let [rec (assoc (php/warn-record errno msg) :yang.php/refusal refusal)\\\\n    48\\\\t             h (cell/get php.rt/error-handler)]\\\\n    49\\\\t         (if (= h :php/null)\\\\n    50\\\\t           (php/warn-sink rec)\\\\n    51\\\\t           (if (= (php/invoke-handler h errno msg) false)\\\\n    52\\\\t             (php/warn-sink rec)\\\\n    53\\\\t             :php/null))))]\\\\n    54\\\\t    [php/include-missing!\\\\n    55\\\\t     ;; the refusal map follows the base kind; the texts carry the kind as\\\\n    56\\\\t     ;; written; a refused path is never marked included\\\\n    57\\\\t     (fn [path kind refusal]\\\\n    58\\\\t       (let [nm (php/include-kind-name kind)]\\\\n    59\\\\t         (do (php/warn-refusal\\\\n    60\\\\t               2\\\\n    61\\\\t               (data/str-concat\\\\n    62\\\\t                 (data/str-concat (data/str-concat nm \\\\\\\"(\\\\\\\") path)\\\\n    63\\\\t                 \\\\\\\"): Failed to open stream: No such file or directory\\\\\\\")\\\\n    64\\\\t               refusal)\\\\n    65\\\\t             (if (php/include-require? kind)\\\\n    66\\\\t               (php/throw-error\\\\n    67\\\\t                 \\\\\\\"Error\\\\\\\"\\\\n    68\\\\t                 (data/str-concat\\\\n    69\\\\t                   (data/str-concat\\\\n    70\\\\t                     (data/str-concat \\\\\\\"Failed opening required '\\\\\\\" path)\\\\n    71\\\\t                     \\\\\\\"' (include_path='\\\\\\\")\\\\n    72\\\\t                   (data/str-concat php/include-path \\\\\\\"')\\\\\\\")))\\\\n    73\\\\t               (do (php/warn-refusal\\\\n    74\\\\t                     2\\\\n    75\\\\t                     (data/str-concat\\\\n    76\\\\t                       (data/str-concat\\\\n    77\\\\t                         (data/str-concat\\\\n    78\\\\t                           (data/str-concat nm \\\\\\\"(): Failed opening '\\\\\\\")\\\\n    79\\\\t                           path)\\\\n    80\\\\t                         \\\\\\\"' for inclusion (include_path='\\\\\\\")\\\\n    81\\\\t                       (data/str-concat php/include-path \\\\\\\"')\\\\\\\"))\\\\n    82\\\\t                     refusal)\\\\n    83\\\\t                   false)))))]\\\\n    84\\\\t    [php/include-body\\\\n    85\\\\t     ;; marks the path before the body runs, names the unit while it runs,\\\\n    86\\\\t     ;; answers the body's `return` value, else 1\\\\n    87\\\\t     (fn [path delivered scope ctx]\\\\n    88\\\\t       (let [prev (cell/get php.rt/unit)]\\\\n    89\\\\t         (do (cell/set! php.rt/included (assoc (cell/get php.rt/included) path true))\\\\n    90\\\\t             (cell/set! php.rt/unit path)\\\\n    91\\\\t             (php/try-finally\\\\n    92\\\\t               (fn []\\\\n    93\\\\t                 (let [v ((get delivered :body) scope ctx)]\\\\n    94\\\\t                   (if (= v :php/no-return) 1 v)))\\\\n    95\\\\t               (fn [x] (cell/set! php.rt/unit prev))))))]\\\\n    96\\\\t    [php/include-run\\\\n    97\\\\t     ;; `thunk` answers {:status :ok :body b} or the structured refusal\\\\n    98\\\\t     (fn [path thunk kind scope ctx]\\\\n    99\\\\t       (if (if (php/include-once? kind)\\\\n   100\\\\t             (not (nil? (get (cell/get php.rt/included) path)))\\\\n   101\\\\t             false)\\\\n   102\\\\t         true\\\\n   103\\\\t         (let [r (thunk)]\\\\n   104\\\\t           (if (= (get r :status) :ok)\\\\n   105\\\\t             (php/include-body path r scope ctx)\\\\n   106\\\\t             (php/include-missing! path kind r)))))]\\\\n   107\\\\t    [php/normalize-path\\\\n   108\\\\t     ;; the computed arm's lookup key: leading \\\\\\\"./\\\\\\\" segments dropped\\\\n   109\\\\t     (fn [s]\\\\n   110\\\\t       (if (if (>= (data/str-length s) 2) (= (data/substring s 0 2) \\\\\\\"./\\\\\\\") false)\\\\n   111\\\\t         (php/normalize-path (data/substring s 2))\\\\n   112\\\\t         s))]\\\\n   113\\\\t    [php/include-computed\\\\n   114\\\\t     ;; a computed path is a run-time lookup in the published path map; a\\\\n   115\\\\t     ;; miss is the run-time missing-include behaviour for the kind\\\\n   116\\\\t     (fn [pathv kind scope ctx]\\\\n   117\\\\t       (let [path (php/normalize-path (php/to-string pathv))\\\\n   118\\\\t             thunk (get (cell/get php.rt/path-map) path)]\\\\n   119\\\\t         (php/include-run\\\\n   120\\\\t           path\\\\n   121\\\\t           (if (nil? thunk)\\\\n   122\\\\t             (fn []\\\\n   123\\\\t               (assoc (assoc {} :status :refused)\\\\n   124\\\\t                      :reason :yang.php/computed-path-unmapped))\\\\n   125\\\\t             thunk)\\\\n   126\\\\t           kind\\\\n   127\\\\t           scope\\\\n   128\\\\t           ctx)))]\\\\n   129\\\\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- scopes\\\\n   130\\\\t    ;; An including scope is `:php/globals` (the entry unit's top level) or a\\\\n   131\\\\t    ;; scope cell: name to the variable's own cell, in insertion order. A\\\\n   132\\\\t    ;; dynamic-profile function adopts the cells its body already holds, so an\\\\n   133\\\\t    ;; included body and the function see one variable.\\\\n   134\\\\t    [php/scope-new\\\\n   135\\\\t     (fn [] (cell/new (assoc (assoc {} :cells {}) :order [])))]\\\\n   136\\\\t    [php/scope-adopt!\\\\n   137\\\\t     (fn [d name c]\\\\n   138\\\\t       (let [s (cell/get d)]\\\\n   139\\\\t         (do (cell/set! d (assoc (assoc s :cells (assoc (get s :cells) name c))\\\\n   140\\\\t                                 :order (php/vconj (get s :order) name)))\\\\n   141\\\\t             c)))]\\\\n   142\\\\t    [php/scope-cell\\\\n   143\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   144\\\\t       (let [c (get (get (cell/get d) :cells) name)]\\\\n   145\\\\t         (if (nil? c) (php/scope-adopt! d name (cell/new :php/undef)) c)))]\\\\n   146\\\\t    [php/scope-release-loop\\\\n   147\\\\t     (fn [cells order i]\\\\n   148\\\\t       (if (< i (data/count order))\\\\n   149\\\\t         (do (php/unset-cv (get cells (get order i)))\\\\n   150\\\\t             (php/scope-release-loop cells order (+ i 1)))\\\\n   151\\\\t         (php/flush-pending!)))]\\\\n   152\\\\t    [php/scope-release!\\\\n   153\\\\t     (fn [d] (let [s (cell/get d)] (php/scope-release-loop (get s :cells) (get s :order) 0)))]\\\\n   154\\\\t    [php/dict-get\\\\n   155\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   156\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-get name) (php/local-get (php/scope-cell d name) name)))]\\\\n   157\\\\t    [php/dict-peek\\\\n   158\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   159\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-peek name) (php/local-peek (php/scope-cell d name))))]\\\\n   160\\\\t    [php/dict-set!\\\\n   161\\\\t     (fn [d name v]\\\\n   162\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-set! name v) (php/local-set! (php/scope-cell d name) v)))]\\\\n   163\\\\t    [php/dict-put!\\\\n   164\\\\t     (fn [d name v]\\\\n   165\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-put! name v) (php/local-put! (php/scope-cell d name) v)))]\\\\n   166\\\\t    [php/dict-make-ref!\\\\n   167\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   168\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-make-ref! name) (php/make-ref-cv (php/scope-cell d name))))]\\\\n   169\\\\t    [php/dict-bind!\\\\n   170\\\\t     (fn [d name m]\\\\n   171\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-bind! name m) (php/bind-marker (php/scope-cell d name) m)))]\\\\n   172\\\\t    [php/dict-isset?\\\\n   173\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   174\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-isset? name) (php/local-isset? (php/scope-cell d name))))]\\\\n   175\\\\t    [php/dict-unset!\\\\n   176\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   177\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-unset! name) (php/local-unset! (php/scope-cell d name))))]\\\\n   178\\\\t    [php/dict-capture\\\\n   179\\\\t     (fn [d name]\\\\n   180\\\\t       (if (= d :php/globals) (php/global-capture name) (php/local-capture (php/scope-cell d name))))]\\\\n   181\\\\t    [php/name-start?\\\\n   182\\\\t     (fn [c]\\\\n   183\\\\t       (if (if (>= c 97) (<= c 122) false) true\\\\n   184\\\\t           (if (if (>= c 65) (<= c 90) false) true (if (= c 95) true (>= c 128)))))]\\\\n   185\\\\t    [php/name-rest?\\\\n   186\\\\t     (fn [c] (if (php/name-start? c) true (if (>= c 48) (<= c 57) false)))]\\\\n   187\\\\t    [php/valid-name-at\\\\n   188\\\\t     (fn [cs i n]\\\\n   189\\\\t       (if (< i n) (if (php/name-rest? (get cs i)) (php/valid-name-at cs (+ i 1) n) false) true))]\\\\n   190\\\\t    [php/valid-name?\\\\n   191\\\\t     (fn [s]\\\\n   192\\\\t       (let [cs (data/str->code-points s) n (data/count cs)]\\\\n   193\\\\t         (if (= n 0) false (if (php/name-start? (get cs 0)) (php/valid-name-at cs 1 n) false))))]\\\\n   194\\\\t    [php/extract-loop\\\\n   195\\\\t     (fn [d arr flags prefix i n count]\\\\n   196\\\\t       (if (< i n)\\\\n   197\\\\t         (let [k (get (php/array-order arr) i)\\\\n   198\\\\t               base (php/to-string k)\\\\n   199\\\\t               name (if (= flags 3) (data/str-concat prefix base)\\\\n   200\\\\t                        (if (if (= flags 2) (php/dict-isset? d base) false)\\\\n   201\\\\t                          (data/str-concat prefix base) base))\\\\n   202\\\\t               write? (if (php/valid-name? name)\\\\n   203\\\\t                        (if (= flags 1) (not (php/dict-isset? d base)) true)\\\\n   204\\\\t                        false)]\\\\n   205\\\\t           (do (if write? (php/dict-set! d name (php/addref (php/array-get arr k))) :php/null)\\\\n   206\\\\t               (php/extract-loop d arr flags prefix (+ i 1) n (if write? (+ count 1) count))))\\\\n   207\\\\t         count))]\\\\n   208\\\\t    [php/bi-extract\\\\n   209\\\\t     (fn [args d]\\\\n   210\\\\t       (do (php/arity-between \\\\\\\"extract\\\\\\\" args 1 3 \\\\\\\"at least 1\\\\\\\")\\\\n   211\\\\t           (let [arr (php/arg-array (get args 0) \\\\\\\"extract\\\\\\\" 1 \\\\\\\"array\\\\\\\")\\\\n   212\\\\t                 flags (php/to-int (php/arg-or args 1 0))]\\\\n   213\\\\t             (if (= (integer/bit-and flags 256) 256)\\\\n   214\\\\t               (php/throw-error \\\\\\\"Error\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"extract(EXTR_REFS) is not supported (corner C11)\\\\\\\")\\\\n   215\\\\t               (php/extract-loop d arr flags (php/to-string (php/arg-or args 2 \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"))\\\\n   216\\\\t                                 0 (php/array-count arr) 0)))))]\\\\n   217\\\\t    [php/compact-name\\\\n   218\\\\t     (fn [d name out]\\\\n   219\\\\t       (let [nm (php/to-string name)]\\\\n   220\\\\t         (if (php/dict-isset? d nm) (php/array-put out nm (php/addref (php/dict-peek d nm))) out)))]\\\\n   221\\\\t    [php/compact-arg\\\\n   222\\\\t     (fn [d v out]\\\\n   223\\\\t       (if (= (php/kind v) :array)\\\\n   224\\\\t         (php/compact-array d v 0 (php/array-count v) out)\\\\n   225\\\\t         (php/compact-name d v out)))]\\\\n   226\\\\t    [php/compact-array\\\\n   227\\\\t     (fn [d arr i n out]\\\\n   228\\\\t       (if (< i n)\\\\n   229\\\\t         (php/compact-array d arr (+ i 1) n\\\\n   230\\\\t                            (php/compact-arg d (php/array-get arr (get (php/array-order arr) i)) out))\\\\n   231\\\\t         out))]\\\\n   232\\\\t    [php/compact-loop\\\\n   233\\\\t     (fn [d args i n out]\\\\n   234\\\\t       (if (< i n) (php/compact-loop d args (+ i 1) n (php/compact-arg d (get args i) out)) out))]\\\\n   235\\\\t    [php/bi-compact\\\\n   236\\\\t     (fn [args d]\\\\n   237\\\\t       (do (php/arity-between \\\\\\\"compact\\\\\\\" args 1 1000000 \\\\\\\"at least 1\\\\\\\")\\\\n   238\\\\t           (php/compact-loop d args 0 (data/count args) (php/empty-array))))]\\\\n   239\\\\t    [php/ctx-this\\\\n   240\\\\t     (fn [f]\\\\n   241\\\\t       (if (= f :php/null)\\\\n   242\\\\t         (php/throw-error \\\\\\\"Error\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"Using $this when not in object context\\\\\\\")\\\\n   243\\\\t         (php/this-of f)))]\\\\n   244\\\\t    [php/ctx-this-or-null\\\\n   245\\\\t     (fn [f] (if (= f :php/null) :php/null (php/this-or-null f)))]\\\\n   246\\\\t    [php/ctx-has-this?\\\\n   247\\\\t     (fn [f] (if (= f :php/null) false (php/has-this? f)))]\\\\n   248\\\\t    [php/bind-path-map!\\\\n   249\\\\t     (fn [m] (cell/set! php.rt/path-map m))]\\\\n   250\\\\t    [php/bind-class-map!\\\\n   251\\\\t     ;; the composition's `phpm.$classmap` exports: lower-cased class name to\\\\n   252\\\\t     ;; path, and the literal paths a computed include may name\\\\n   253\\\\t     (fn [classes paths]\\\\n   254\\\\t       (do (cell/set! php.rt/class-map classes)\\\\n   255\\\\t           (cell/set! php.rt/path-map paths)))]\\\\n   256\\\\t    ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- namespaces\\\\n   257\\\\t    [php/resolve-fn2\\\\n   258\\\\t     ;; the two-key lookup of an unqualified call inside a namespace\\\\n   259\\\\t     (fn [lc1 lc2 written]\\\\n   260\\\\t       (let [f (get (cell/get php.rt/functions) lc1)]\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_21\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '590,785p;1250,1323p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '2147,2190p;5065,5100p;5245,5298p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_21\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '590,785p;1250,1323p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '2147,2190p;5065,5100p;5245,5298p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"   590\\\\t  [name]\\\\n   591\\\\t  (subs name 1))\\\\n   592\\\\t\\\\n   593\\\\t\\\\n   594\\\\t(defn- checked-var\\\\n   595\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`name`; `$this` is read through the running method's function cell.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   596\\\\t  [_n name]\\\\n   597\\\\t  name)\\\\n   598\\\\t\\\\n   599\\\\t\\\\n   600\\\\t(defn- cc-node\\\\n   601\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The calling class: the method's lexical `%cc`, null outside a class.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   602\\\\t  [ctx]\\\\n   603\\\\t  (if (:cc ctx) (u/v '%cc) (u/lit :php/null)))\\\\n   604\\\\t\\\\n   605\\\\t\\\\n   606\\\\t(defn- this-var?\\\\n   607\\\\t  [name]\\\\n   608\\\\t  (= \\\\\\\"$this\\\\\\\" name))\\\\n   609\\\\t\\\\n   610\\\\t\\\\n   611\\\\t(defn- this-node\\\\n   612\\\\t  [ctx]\\\\n   613\\\\t  (cond\\\\n   614\\\\t    (:fn ctx) (app* 'php/this-of (u/v '%fn))\\\\n   615\\\\t    (:module? ctx) (app* 'php/ctx-this (u/v '%ctx))\\\\n   616\\\\t    :else (app* 'php/throw-error (u/lit \\\\\\\"Error\\\\\\\") (u/lit \\\\\\\"Using $this when not in object context\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n   617\\\\t\\\\n   618\\\\t\\\\n   619\\\\t(declare chain-calls member-vis class-ref-node class-name-node leftmost-token-text lower-class lower-new\\\\n   620\\\\t         lower-class-constant lower-initializer-part class-spec*)\\\\n   621\\\\t\\\\n   622\\\\t\\\\n   623\\\\t(defn- static-var?\\\\n   624\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A