 101\\\\t\\\\n   102\\\\t### 3.1 Reference runtime\\\\n   103\\\\t\\\\n   104\\\\tPHP 8.3 CLI at a pinned patch release (owner decision B8.1), with `php.ini`\\\\n   105\\\\tpinning `precision=14`, `serialize_precision=-1`, `error_reporting=E_ALL` and\\\\n   106\\\\t`display_errors=stderr`. The grammar's feature set (enums, `match`,\\\\n   107\\\\t`readonly`, named arguments, attributes) is PHP 8.1 and later, so 8.3 is the\\\\n   108\\\\tnatural pin. PHP 8.4 features (property hooks, asymmetric visibility) are not\\\\n   109\\\\tparsed (corner C10).\\\\n  2433\\\\t|                     | filesystem lookup is not.           | supported        |\\\\n  2434\\\\t+---------------------+-------------------------------------+------------------+\\\\n  2435\\\\t\\\\n  2436\\\\t### 17.3 Convergence and the blocking rule\\\\n  2437\\\\t\\\\n  2438\\\\t**Claimed rows are normative, and a known-incorrect claimed row blocks.** A\\\\n  2439\\\\trow of the transition table is a statement of Zend's behaviour, fixed from the\\\\n  2440\\\\thandler source and **confirmed by the oracle before the slice that claims it\\\\n  2441\\\\tlands**. After landing, a disagreement between a row and the pinned PHP CLI is\\\\n  2442\\\\ta defect of the row, never of the fixture. A finding that a claimed row\\\\n  2443\\\\tcontradicts Zend blocks landing of any slice whose support profile includes\\\\n  2444\\\\tthat row until either the row is corrected (and its fixture regenerated from\\\\n  2445\\\\tthe oracle), or the Architect explicitly moves the behaviour to section 17.2\\\\n  2446\\\\tas a restricted corner with a departure fixture whose expected value is the\\\\n  2447\\\\trecorded deviation, with the owner's acceptance when the corner touches a\\\\n  2448\\\\tPhase 3 exit criterion. Regenerating a fixture to match an incorrect row is\\\\n  2449\\\\tforbidden: oracle fixtures pin behaviour; they do not legitimize a\\\\n  2450\\\\tcontradictory normative rule.\\\\n  2451\\\\t\\\\n  2452\\\\tT