age (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\\\\n     3\\\\t   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\\\\n     4\\\\t   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\\\\n     5\\\\t   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\\\\n     6\\\\t   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\\\\n     7\\\\t   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\\\\n     8\\\\t   what a safepoint is.\\\\n     9\\\\t\\\\n    10\\\\t   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\\\\n    11\\\\t     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\\\\n    12\\\\t     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\\\\n    13\\\\t     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\\\\n    14\\\\t   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\\\\n    15\\\\t     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\\\\n    16\\\\t     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\\\\n    17\\\\t     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\\\\n    18\\\\t     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\\\\n    19\\\\t   - A mark's value is a kind, or a vector `[kind datum ...]`: the data\\\\n    20\\\\t     (a function's name and line, a statement's line) are literals the\\\\n    21\\\\t     frontend knows and the derived tree may need. A profile entry is a\\\\n    22\\\\t     hook symbol, or `{:hook symbol :operands true}` to apply the hook to\\\\n    23\\\\t     the mark's data. A statement kind (`statement-kinds`: `:line`) marks\\\\n    24\\\\t     any node, not a lambda; its hook is applied before the node, which\\\\n    25\\\\t     is sequenced after it.\\\\n    26\\\\t   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\\\\n    27\\\\t     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\\\\n    28\\\\t     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\\\\n    29\\\\t   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\\\\n    30\\\\t     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\\\\n    31\\\\t     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\\\\n    32\\\\t     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\\\\n    33\\\\t     same record.\\\\n    34\\\\t   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\\\\n    35\\\\t     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\\\\n    36\\\\t     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\\\\n    37\\\\t     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    38\\\\t  (:require\\\\n    39\\\\t    [dao.jing :as jing]\\\\n    40\\\\t    [yang.stage :as stage]\\\\n    41\\\\t    [yang.tails :as tails]\\\\n    42\\\\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\\\\n    43\\\\t\\\\n    44\\\\t\\\\n    45\\\\t(def binder\\\\n    46\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The parameter of every inserted sequencing lambda.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    47\\\\t  'yang.safepoint/_)\\\\n    48\\\\t\\\\n    49\\\\t\\\\n    50\\\\t(def function\\\\n    51\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The `:yin.ledger/function` of a safepoint derivation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    52\\\\t  :yang.safepoint/insert)\\\\n    53\\\\t\\\\n    54\\\\t\\\\n    55\\\\t(def site-key\\\\n    56\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The frontend-metadata key a site mark travels under.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    57\\\\t  :yang/site)\\\\n    58\\\\t\\\\n    59\\\\t\\\\n    60\\\\t(defn sites\\\\n    61\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`{path mark}` (a kind, or `[kind datum ...]`) of every site marked in the frontend-metadata relation\\\\n    62\\\\t   `metadata` at occurrence `origin` of tree `root`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    63\\\\t  [metadata origin root]\\\\n    64\\\\t  (into {}\\\\n    65\\\\t        (keep (fn [[o r path k v]]\\\\n    66\\\\t                (when (and (= o origin) (= r root) (= k site-key))\\\\n    67\\\\t                  [path v])))\\\\n    68\\\\t        metadata))\\\\n    69\\\\t\\\\n    70\\\\t\\\\n    71\\\\t(defn site-set\\\\n    72\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The selected sites as a sorted vector of `[path mark]`, a mark a kind or `[kind datum ...]`, in an order every\\\\n    73\\\\t   host computes alike.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    74\\\\t  [selected]\\\\n    75\\\\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str (map vec selected))))\\\\n    76\\\\t\\\\n    77\\\\t\\\\n    78\\\\t(def exit-kinds\\\\n    79\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Exit kind -> the entry kind whose sites it wraps. An exit hook is applied\\\\n    80\\\\t   to the value of the site's body, so it runs after a normal exit and its\\\\n    81\\\\t   answer is the body's value; an escape out of the body skips it.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    82\\\\t  {:return :call})\\\\n    83\\\\t\\\\n    84\\\\t\\\\n    85\\\\t(def statement-kinds\\\\n    86\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Kinds whose sites are any node, not a lambda: the hook runs before the\\\\n    87\\\\t   node, and the node's value is the site's.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    88\\\\t  #{:line})\\\\n    89\\\\t\\\\n    90\\\\t\\\\n    91\\\\t(defn- mark-kind\\\\n    92\\\\t  [mark]\\\\n    93\\\\t  (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark))\\\\n    94\\\\t\\\\n    95\\\\t\\\\n    96\\\\t(defn- entry-hook\\\\n    97\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The `{:hook sym :operands [literal ...]}` of profile entry `entry` at a\\\\n    98\\\\t   site marked `mark`, or nil.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    99\\\\t  [entry mark]\\\\n   100\\\\t  (when entry\\\\n   101\\\\t    (if (map? entry)\\\\n   102\\\\t      {:hook (:hook entry),\\\\n   103\\\\t       :operands (when (:operands entry) (vec (rest mark)))}\\\\n   104\\\\t      {:hook entry})))\\\\n   105\\\\t\\\\n   106\\\\t\\\\n   107\\\\t(defn- site-hooks\\\\n   108\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`{:enter h :exit h}` (either absent), each an `entry-hook`, for a site\\\\n   109\\\\t   marked `mark` under `profile`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   110\\\\t  [profile mark]\\\\n   111\\\\t  (let [kind (mark-kind mark)\\\\n   112\\\\t        exit (some (fn [[x entry]] (when (= entry kind) (get profile x)))\\\\n   113\\\\t                   exit-kinds)]\\\\n   114\\\\t    (cond-> {}\\\\n   115\\\\t      (get profile kind) (assoc :enter (entry-hook (get profile kind) mark))\\\\n   116\\\\t      (and (map? (get profile kind)) (:sequence (get profile kind)))\\\\n   117\\\\t      (assoc :sequence? true)\\\\n   118\\\\t      exit (assoc :exit (entry-hook exit mark)))))\\\\n   119\\\\t\\\\n   120\\\\t\\\\n   121\\\\t(defn- hook-application\\\\n   122\\\\t  [{:keys [hook operands]} args]\\\\n   123\\\\t  {:type :application,\\\\n   124\\\\t   :operator {:type :variable, :name hook},\\\\n   125\\\\t   :operands (into (mapv (fn [x] {:type :literal, :value x}) operands) args)})\\\\n   126\\\\t\\\\n   127\\\\t\\\\n   128\\\\t(defn- sequence-hook\\\\n   129\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`node` evaluated after `hook` is applied.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   130\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\n   131\\\\t  {:type :application,\\\\n   132\\\\t   :operator {:type :lambda, :params [binder], :body node},\\\\n   133\\\\t   :operands [(hook-application hook [])]})\\\\n   134\\\\t\\\\n   135\\\\t\\\\n   136\\\\t(defn- prefix-hook\\\\n   137\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied before its body runs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   138\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\n   139\\\\t  (assoc node\\\\n   140\\\\t         :body (sequence-hook (:body node) hook)))\\\\n   141\\\\t\\\\n   142\\\\t\\\\n   143\\\\t(defn- wrap-hook\\\\n   144\\\\t  \\\\\\\"Lambda `node` with `hook` applied to its body's value.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   145\\\\t  [node hook]\\\\n   146\\\\t  (assoc node :body (hook-application hook [(:body node)])))\\\\n   147\\\\t\\\\n   148\\\\t\\\\n   149\\\\t(defn- rewrite\\\\n   150\\\\t  \\\\\\\"The map AST `ast` with each `{path {:enter h :exit h}}` site's exit hook\\\\n   151\\\\t   wrapped around its body and its entry hook prefixed. Throws when a site\\\\n   152\\\\t   names no node, or a node that is not a lambda.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   153\\\\t  [ast hooks]\\\\n   154\\\\t  (let [seen (volatile! #{})]\\\\n   155\\\\t    (letfn [(walk\\\\n   156\\\\t              [node path]\\\\n   157\\\\t              (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node))\\\\n   158\\\\t                    node (reduce\\\\n   159\\\\t                           (fn [n [j [field kind]]]\\\\n   160\\\\t                             (let [pos (+ j 2)]\\\\n  2735\\\\t             :value (:val effect),\\\\n  2736\\\\t             :blocked? false})\\\\n  2737\\\\t          (let [[id s'] (gensym state \\\\\\\"effect\\\\\\\")\\\\n  2738\\\\t                handler (module/get-effect-handler (:modules state)\\\\n  2739\\\\t                                                   (:effect effect))]\\\\n  2740\\\\t            (if handler\\\\n  2741\\\\t              (handler s' effect (assoc opts :id id))\\\\n  2742\\\\t              (fail \\\\\\\"Unknown effect\\\\\\\" {:effect (:effect effect)}))))]\\\\n  2743\\\\t    (update result\\\\n  2744\\\\t            :state\\\\n  2745\\\\t            (fn [result-state]\\\\n  2746\\\\t              (telemetry/emit-snapshot (assoc result-state\\\\n  2747\\\\t                                              :value (:value result))\\\\n  2748\\\\t                                       :effect\\\\n  2749\\\\t                                       {:effect-type (:effect effect)})))))\\\\n  2750\\\\t\\\\n  2751\\\\t\\\\n  2752\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n  2753\\\\t;; Program Cache Machinery\\\\n  2754\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n  2755\\\\t\\\\n  2756\\\\t(def default-compiled-cache-limit 8)\\\\n  2757\\\\t\\\\n  2758\\\\t\\\\n  2759\\\\t(defn build-program-index\\\\n  2760\\\\t  [datoms]\\\\n  2761\\\\t  (group-by first (vec datoms)))\\\\n  2762\\\\t\\\\n  2763\\\\t\\\\n  2764\\\\t(defn frame-versions\\\\n  2765\\\\t  [frame]\\\\n  2766\\\\t  (loop [f frame\\\\n  2767\\\\t         acc #{}]\\\\n  2768\\\\t    (if (map? f)\\\\n   298\\\\t  effect/make)\\\\n   299\\\\t\\\\n   300\\\\t\\\\n   301\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   302\\\\t;; The `stream` module\\\\n   303\\\\t;; =============================================================================\\\\n   304\\\\t;;\\\\n   305\\\\t;; These are pure effect constructors. They touch no stream: Yin source calls\\\\n   306\\\\t;; them through the module system, they return effects, and the engine\\\\n   307\\\\t;; interprets those. `take!` is deliberately absent: destructive read is one\\\\n   308\\\\t;; reader's progress and every other reader's data loss, and a v2 `take!` would\\\\n   309\\\\t;; need the reader-position-in-the-medium the contract retired.\\\\n   310\\\\t\\\\n   311\\\\t(defn make\\\\n   312\\\\t  ([] (make nil))\\\\n   313\\\\t  ([cap] (make-effect :stream/make {:capacity cap})))\\\\n   314\\\\t\\\\n   315\\\\t\\\\n   316\\\\t(defn put!\\\\n   317\\\\t  [s v]\\\\n   318\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/put {:stream s, :val v}))\\\\n   319\\\\t\\\\n   320\\\\t\\\\n   321\\\\t(defn cursor\\\\n   322\\\\t  [s]\\\\n   323\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/cursor {:stream s}))\\\\n   324\\\\t\\\\n   325\\\\t\\\\n   326\\\\t(defn next!\\\\n   327\\\\t  [c]\\\\n   328\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/next {:cursor c}))\\\\n   329\\\\t\\\\n   330\\\\t\\\\n   331\\\\t(defn poll!\\\\n   332\\\\t  \\\\\\\"`next!` that never parks: `blocked` is the value `:dao.stream/blocked`.\\\\n   333\\\\t   It is its own effect kind, so a callee whose profile omits it cannot\\\\n   334\\\\t   observe whether a read would have waited.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   335\\\\t  [c]\\\\n   336\\\\t  (make-effect :stream/poll {:cursor c}))\\\\n   337\\\\t\\\\n   338\\\\t\\\\n   339\\\\t(defn close!\\\\n   340\\\\t  [s]\\\\n   390\\\\t(defn get-cell\\\\n   391\\\\t  [c]\\\\n   392\\\\t  (make-effect :cell/get {:cell c}))\\\\n   393\\\\t\\\\n   394\\\\t\\\\n   395\\\