 or remote  |\\\\n   500\\\\t|               | in a worker; TypeScript       | service                  |\\\\n   501\\\\t|               | compiled at build             |                          |\\\\n   502\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\n   503\\\\t| Dart / CLJD   | Generated Dart parser (the    | Sidecar where supported, |\\\\n   504\\\\t|               | local implementation for      | or a remote service;     |\\\\n   505\\\\t|               | Python since 2026-10-17; a    | otherwise unsupported    |\\\\n   506\\\\t|               | grammar without a Dart helper | outcome                  |\\\\n   507\\\\t|               | answers `unavailable-parser`) |                          |\\\\n   508\\\\t+---------------+-------------------------------+--------------------------+\\\\n   509\\\\t```\\\\n   510\\\\t\\\\n   511\\\\tA CLJD application can compile through a service without bundling ANTLR.\\\\n   512\\\\tIt can also consume previously compiled rows without any parser.\\\\n   513\\\\t\\\\n   514\\\\tFull offline local compilation on all three hosts requires validated\\\\n   515\\\\tparser artifacts for all three. Service-based portability must not be\\\\n   516\\\\tadvertised as offline portability.\\\\n  4380\\\\treporting is supplied by a listener, while recovery may insert/delete\\\\n  4381\\\\ttokens, continue, or raise recognition errors. The integration must\\\\n  4382\\\\tcontrol both mechanisms.\\\\n  4383\\\\t\\\\n  4384\\\\t### 10.1 Boundary policy\\\\n  4385\\\\t\\\\n  4386\\\\tFor lexer and parser:\\\\n  4387\\\\t\\\\n  4388\\\\t1. Remove default console listeners.\\\\n  4389\\\\t2. Install boundary transformations that classify diagnostics as plain\\\\n  4390\\\\t   data.\\\\n  4391\\\\t3. Select a pinned recovery strategy.\\\\n  4392\\\\t4. Catch recognized parsing failures at the host boundary.\\\\n  4393\\\\t5. Export recovery markers and terminal parse status.\\\\n  4394\\\\t6. Retain no exception, recognizer, token, or host stack object in\\\\n  4395\\\\t   payloads.\\\\n  4396\\\\t\\\\n  4397\\\\tA default strict profile refuses executable publication after any\\\\n  4398\\\\tlexical or syntax error, even when ANTLR constructed a recovered CST. An\\\\n  4399\\\\tIDE profile may publish partial syntax for tooling on a separate medium.\\\\n  4400\\\\t\\\\n  4401\\\\tWorker crashes, timeouts, resource exhaustion, grammar incompatibility,\\\\n  4402\\\\tand internal defects remain distinct from invalid source.\\\\n  4403\\\\t\\\\n  4404\\\\t### 10.2 Qualified outcome maps\\\\n  4405\\\\t\\\\n  4406\\\\tEvery stage reports through qualified outcome maps in the shape of\\\\n  4407\\\\tsection 6.2: a stream outcome wrapping a compiler outcome. The compiler\\\\n  4408\\\\toutcome names its phase and reason with qualified keywords:\\\\n  4409\\\\t\\\\n  4410\\\\t- Parse errors: `:yang.compile/syntax-error` from the parse phase.\\\\n  4411\\\\t- Semantic errors: unbound names, type errors, unsupported features,\\\\n  4412\\\\t  from the analyze phase.\\\\n  4413\\\\t- Lowering failures: unhandled CST constructs, grammar/profile mismatch,\\\\n  4414\\\\t  from the lower phase.\\\\n  4415\\\\t- Operational failures: worker crash, timeout, cancellation, resource\\\\n  4416\\\\t  limit, reported as operational events and never as language errors.\\\\n  4417\\\\t\\\\n  4418\\\\t### 10.3 Proposed diagnostic record\\\\n  4419\\\\t\\\\n  4420\\\\t```clojure\\\\n  4421\\\\t{:yang.diagnostic/code :yang.python/unbound-local\\\\n  4422\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/phase :yang.compile/analyze\\\\n  4423\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/severity :yang.diagnostic/error\\\\n  4424\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/request [\\\\\\\"client-token\\\\\\\" 12]\\\\n  4425\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/attempt [\\\\\\\"worker-token\\\\\\\" 4]\\\\n  4426\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/source [\\\\\\\"source-unit\\\\\\\" 3]\\\\n  4427\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/span {:start-byte 41 :end-byte 42}\\\\n  4428\\\\t :yang.diagnostic/argum