ction 15) are implemented on\\\\n     4\\\\tthe `yang.php.antlr` route (P2: arrays, key coercion, `foreach` by value, the\\\\n     5\\\\tcore array builtins and sorting, oracle-verified against `php-8.3.35`, section\\\\n     6\\\\t17.3). P3 landed in two parts: P3-a (the counted-cell substrate and the\\\\n     7\\\\tprelude-level reference model, merged earlier) and P3-b (the program-level\\\\n     8\\\\tlowering, see \\\\\\\"P3-b landing status\\\\\\\" below). P4 and P5 are complete; P6 is in\\\\n     9\\\\tprogress through the linked inclusion profile, dynamic scope, namespaces,\\\\n    10\\\\tconstants and autoload class map. P6's oracle recording and three-host DHT\\\\n    11\\\\tverification remain part of its landing. The legacy `yang/php.cljc` frontend\\\\n    12\\\\tis still the installed one. Design by Fable (Lead\\\\n    13\\\\tSystem Architect seat); adversarial review by codex (gpt-6.1-sol) over a\\\\n    14\\\\tnine-round design loop that ended READY with sign-off granted. Section 20\\\\n    15\\\\t(\\\\\\\"Design provenance\\\\\\\") cites the loop.\\\\n    16\\\\t\\\\n    17\\\\t**P3-b landing status.** The program-level lowering of the P3 plan (steps S2 to\\\\n    18\\\\tS12) lands on branch `yang-php-p3b`; the oracle is the pinned `php-8.3.35`\\\\n    19\\\\t(`php:8.3-cli` on shiva, banner `php-8.3.35 shiva 2026-10-25`).\\\\n    20\\\\t\\\\n    21\\\\t- Lowered and oracle-pinned: references (`=&` in every location form,\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_40\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"One more gap belongs in the implementation plan: `try-require` returns a module name, not an export callable. I’ll specify a small, profiled accessor for an already installed export to complete the handoff. I’ll also keep redeclaration timing, method context, eval-local statics, and diagnostic locations pending until the PHP 8.3.35 oracle pin